// A name folded into a module by its wildcard import, reached through that
// module's qualifier from a module loaded before it -- and refused, although
// that module is not the root.
//
// The third of the load-order trio (module-nameres-transit.cone says what is
// pinned and why). It exists to separate two readings of the root's failure:
// that the root is special, or that load order is what decides. moduleearly is
// added to the program when its parse begins, before its own 'import
// moduletransit' loads moduletransit, so it is resolved first and fails
// exactly as the root does. The annotation is in moduleearly.cone, where the
// compiler reports the diagnostic; this file has none of its own.
//
// The imported modules are moduleearly.cone and, through it, moduletransit.cone
// and modulesub.cone.

import moduleearly;

fn viaEarly() i64 {
  moduleearly.viaMid(1i64);
}
